1.
| Topic                         | What it means in our project                                                                                                                                                                  |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Role-based collaboration**  | Each agent has one specific responsibility (Intake, Policy, Approval).                                                                                                                        |
| **Supervisor–Worker pattern** | The workflow/controller acts as the supervisor and delegates work to worker agents.                                                                                                           |
| **Communication channels**    | Agents pass structured information (messages/JSON) to each other.                                                                                                                             |
| **Agent isolation**           | Each agent only knows what it needs to know and doesn't perform another agent's job.                                                                                                          |
| **Event-driven agents**       | A new purchase request triggers the workflow, causing agents to run in sequence.                                                                                                              |
| **A2A (Agent2Agent)**         | One agent sends its result directly to another agent.                                                                                                                                         |
| **MCP**                       | A standard way for agents to access external tools or resources. We may not need a full MCP server for this assignment, but I'll explain where it fits and whether it should be demonstrated. |

2.

What happens internally?
Purchase Request
        │
        ▼
Intake Agent
        │
Reads system prompt
        │
Reads purchase request
        │
Combines both
        │
Sends to Groq
        │
Returns structured response

Notice something important.

The LLM receives two things:

System Prompt
+
User Request

Not just the purchase request.

That's why changing only the system prompt completely changes the agent's behavior.

3.

Are we implementing the official Google A2A Protocol?

No.

This is an important distinction for your understanding.

Your assignment lists A2A Protocol as a concept.

Right now we're implementing the idea of Agent-to-Agent communication:

Agent A

↓

Agent B

The official A2A Protocol (introduced by Google) defines standardized message formats and discovery mechanisms between independent agents. It's a broader interoperability standard.

For this assignment, passing structured information from one AutoGen agent to another is enough to demonstrate the concept unless your instructor explicitly requires the official protocol implementation.

This distinction will impress your evaluator if they ask.

4.
This is an important engineering lesson

You will hear this sentence a lot:

LLMs talk naturally to humans.

Agents should talk structurally to other agents. aka json.

